From: alarm-diting <alarm@diting>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Separate the TX
 SoundWire ports of the two microphones

With codec ports 1 and 2 both on master port 1, ADC1 and ADC4 are sent
in the same bit slot and the capture is white noise. Codec port 2 goes
to master port 2, so ADC4 arrives on TX macro input SWR_MIC5, and the
DAPM route has to follow, otherwise ADC4 and MIC BIAS4 stay off.

The master ports then take the lanes and offsets of the vendor kernel
(qcom,swr-tx-port-params of the diting overlay, use case 0 for the
9.6 MHz bus clock of ADC_NORMAL): port 1 on data lane 1, port 2 on data
lane 2, both at offset 0. With both ports on lane 1 at offsets 0 and 1,
the two microphones still collided on some boots (hiss on both
channels).
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts	2026-10-26 14:53:06.970849931 +0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts	2026-10-26 15:14:14.314336701 +0300
@@ -1057,7 +1057,7 @@
 	audio-routing = "AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
 			"AMIC5", "MIC BIAS4",
 			"TX SWR_INPUT0", "ADC1_OUTPUT",
-			"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC4_OUTPUT";
+			"TX SWR_INPUT5", "ADC4_OUTPUT";
 
 	speaker-playback-dai-link {
 		link-name = "Speaker Playback";
@@ -1111,12 +1111,21 @@
 };
 
 &swr2 {
+	/*
+	 * AMIC1 (ADC1, codec port 1) and AMIC5 (ADC4, codec port 2) are used
+	 * together. Codec port 2 goes to master port 2 (ADC4 is then TX
+	 * SWR_INPUT5), and each port gets its own data lane, as the vendor
+	 * kernel does at 9.6 MHz: port 1 on lane 1 (gpio2), port 2 on lane 2
+	 * (gpio14). Sharing lane 1 at offsets 0 and 1 gave hiss on some boots.
+	 */
+	qcom,ports-offset1 = /bits/ 8 <0x00 0x00 0x01 0x01>;
+	qcom,ports-lane-control = /bits/ 8 <0x01 0x02 0x00 0x00>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 		compatible = "sdw20217010d00";
 		reg = <0 3>;
-		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 1 2 3>;
+		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 2 3 4>;
 	};
 };
 
